# NumbersareFun (NAF)

Follow project skills for detail (always-on):

- `naf-plan-before-build` — when to create `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`
- `naf-legacy-boot-guard` — where code lives; keep `src/game/legacy-boot.js` thin
- `naf-game-domains` — subsystem → file map in `reference.md`

## Scope

These guardrails apply when editing `src/game/**`, `style.css`, or `index.html`.

## Plan gate (summary)

**Small (no plan):** test/copy/comments only; no mults, costs, timings, unlocks, or save fields; total diff ≤ 25 lines.

**Needs plan:** any balance/save change; diff > 25 lines; 2+ files in one subsystem; refactor/extraction; non-trivial `legacy-boot.js` touch.

**Plans:** `.cursor/plans/<name>.plan.md` only (not new agent plans under `docs/plans/`).

**After implementing a plan:** update `.cursor/skills/naf-game-domains/reference.md`.

Exception: user says implement/execute an existing plan — proceed without a new plan.

## Legacy-boot (summary)

Do not add logic to `legacy-boot.js` except `deps` wiring and orchestration. Prefer `modules/number1/` and domain rules files; extend existing `n1-*-boot.js`; no imports of legacy-boot from children. Multi-layer work: touch rules, boot, and legacy — **legacy stays thinnest**. If a boot file is full, prefer `modules/number1/` over growing legacy.

Before/after legacy-boot edits: `npm run metrics:legacy-boot`.

## Hierarchy

User rules override this file. Do not restate user rules (commits, test minimalism, scope) here.
